{"term":"surname","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:82e703f7b46f82b4f7","definition":"The portion of a person's name that is generally hereditary or treated as an indicator of a person's family, which may be shared with other members of the family, or otherwise derived from their names in some fashion; distinguished from that person's given name(s).","example":"James is my first name, and Smith is my surname.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["byname","cognomen","family name","last name","surname","to-name"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["occupational surname","surnameless","surnamey","surnominal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surname#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a104b4ba6ce307a250","definition":"Synonym of epithet, an additional name, particularly those derived from a birthplace, quality, or achievement.","example":"Barsabas (whose syrname was Iustus).","pos":"noun","synonyms":["epithet"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["occupational surname","surnameless","surnamey","surnominal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surname#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:df228c28627042f018","definition":"Synonym of nickname, an additional name given to a person, place, or thing, a byname.","example":"I have before declared that Baal was the Sun, and Baal Peor, a sirname, from a particular place of his worship.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["nickname"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["occupational surname","surnameless","surnamey","surnominal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surname#English","license":"CC-BY-S